From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PolyOpenFirmware <alex.camilo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] drm/panel: raydium-rm67191: 720x1280 panel for Poly
 Trio C60

The Poly Trio C60 ("Kepler") uses an RM67191-command-compatible 720x1280
LCD, not the 1080x1920 AMOLED module the mainline rm67191 driver targets.
Left unchanged the DRM pipeline forms but the panel shows wrong colours,
a wrong black level and column-inversion stripes. Retarget the driver for
the C60 glass:

 - default mode 720x1280 @ ~65 Hz (79.61 MHz pixel clock; H 720 / hfp 100 /
   hsync 90 / hbp 30, V 1280 / vfp 16 / vsync 5 / vbp 2; negative H/V sync);

 - replace the 1080p AMOLED manufacturer command set with the C60's stock
   vendor init -- a series of DCS long-writes (no 0x3A/0xC2/0xFE writes),
   the Focaltech touch-vendor-id 0x79 calibration variant (read from FT5x06
   register 0xA8 on the bench);

 - drive the link in non-burst SYNC-PULSE video mode (mode_flags 0x215 =
   VIDEO | SYNC_PULSE | HSE | NO_EOT_PACKET); burst produced the wrong
   colours / inversion stripes.

Verified on the bench with a camera in the loop: solid red/green/blue each
render in the correct colour and a black/white checkerboard is clean.

Signed-off-by: Alex Camilo <alex.camilo@gmail.com>
